    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24739" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διά-δῠσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>passing through, passage,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τὼς πόρως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ti.Locr.
					100e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Od.</u>
				50
			</span></i>: metaph. in pl., <i>evasions,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἀδικημάτων,</span>
			 i.e. <i>escape from</i> the consequences of crimes,
				<i><span class="en">
				D.
				24.139
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				94
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Dem.</u>
				6
			</span></i>: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				18.32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in pl.,
				<i>passages, galleries,</i> in mines, etc., <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				5.36
			</span></i>: sg., prob.l. in <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				24.5
			</span></i>; <i>subterranean channel,</i> Demetr.Sceps. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				13.1.43
			</span></i>.</div>
